## 4. Commercial redistribution requires prior written consent

Without the Project Owner's prior written consent in a separate commercial
license, you may not, whether the Software is unchanged, modified, rebranded,
incorporated into another product, or bundled with other software:

- Sell, rent, lease, or license access to or copies of the Software for a fee
  or other commercial consideration.
- Package, repackage, white-label, or distribute the Software as part of a
  paid or otherwise monetized software product, application, or bundle,
  including when the Software is described as a free component.
- Offer the Software's CRM or scheduling functionality to third parties as a
  commercial hosted, managed, or software-as-a-service offering. This includes
  subscriptions, access fees, and offerings monetized through advertising,
  sponsorship, or charges bundled with another product or service.

Renaming the Software, changing its branding, modifying its code, or charging
for another part of a bundle does not remove these restrictions. No showing
of net profit is required for these restrictions to apply.

The internal business use, customer portals, and contractor services expressly
permitted in Section 2 remain permitted. A separate commercial license grants
only the rights the Project Owner holds or is authorized to license; any other
required copyright or third-party permissions must also be obtained.

